# Repository Ownership & Security Review Boundaries
#
# Every path a reviewer would want to see a change to must appear below. A rule
# that matches no file is worse than a missing rule: it reads as coverage and
# reviews nothing. `/SECURITY-ROADMAP.md` was one — the tracked file is
# `SECURITY_ROADMAP.md`, so the register holding the repository's recorded
# vulnerabilities had no owner at all.

# Gitea Actions workflows and security policies
/.gitea/workflows/          @infrastructure-team @security-team
/.gitea/CODEOWNERS          @infrastructure-team @security-team
/scripts/security/          @security-team
/SECURITY.md                @security-team
/SECURITY_ROADMAP.md        @security-team
/security_best_practices_report.md @security-team

# The controls that decide whether a run is allowed to be green. These enforce
# the suppression, coverage and gate-drift policies, so a change here can waive
# a gate as effectively as editing the gate itself.
/scripts/ci/                @infrastructure-team @security-team
/scripts/test-ci.sh         @infrastructure-team @security-team
/scripts/verify-all.sh      @infrastructure-team @security-team
/platform/ci/               @infrastructure-team
/platform/exception-register.yaml @security-team

# The declared budgets and baselines. Each of these files holds numbers that
# decide whether a gate is allowed to be green — a coverage floor, a suppression
# count, a ceiling on undelivered work — so raising one waives a gate as
# effectively as editing the gate. On 2026-08-04 none of them had an owner, and
# `codeowners-contract.test.mjs` only knew the five surfaces someone had typed
# into it by hand. That list is now derived: every tracked `platform/*.yaml`
# must be matched by a rule here, so the next budget file fails the contract
# until somebody owns it.
/platform/coverage-baseline.yaml @qa-team @infrastructure-team
/platform/sast-baseline.yaml @security-team
/platform/image-tag-exceptions.yaml @infrastructure-team @security-team
/platform/route-posture-registry.yaml @security-team @qa-team
/platform/release-lag-budget.yaml @infrastructure-team
/platform/integration-debt-budget.yaml @infrastructure-team
/platform/image-release-baseline.yaml @infrastructure-team
/platform/kill-criteria-baseline.yaml @infrastructure-team @qa-team
/platform/VENTURE.template.yaml @infrastructure-team @qa-team

# Cloud Infrastructure & Kubernetes Configurations
